<section id="sec-conclusion" class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-4xl section-shell prose-shell scroll-mt-24">
  <h2>One Triangle, Five Methods, One Area</h2>
  <p>Every method on this page answers the same question from a different starting point. Legs when you have both perpendicular sides, sine when you have an included angle, inradius and semiperimeter when the incircle is in view, altitude when the hypotenuse and its height are known. Match the mode to your measurements, enter them in the right fields with compatible units, and let the calculator do the arithmetic. Then verify with a second method: two routes to the same number is the surest sign the geometry is right.</p>
